{
  "response": "# Verdict: REJECT\n\n## Summary\nThe `BuggyFileInput` component exhibits critical accessibility failures across semantic HTML, assistive technology communication, error handling, and keyboard user experience. It uses unassociated visual text (`<div>Upload file</div>`) instead of a native `<label>`, fails to associate or announce error messages, omits programmatic invalidity (`aria-invalid`), provides no accessible instructions regarding the 5MB file size constraint, and does not announce state updates to screen reader users when errors occur.\n\n---\n\n## Pre-commitment Predictions\n1. **Missing Label Association**: The input will lack a valid programmatic label (`<label htmlFor=\"...\">`), resulting in generic or missing accessible names.\n2. **Missing Error Association & Live Announcement**: The error message (`error-message`) will not be linked via `aria-describedby` or announced via `aria-live` / `role=\"alert\"`.\n3. **Missing `aria-invalid`**: The input will not convey error state programmatically when validation fails.\n4. **Undisclosed Constraints**: File size limit (5MB) will be enforced purely in code without accessible upfront instructions or descriptions.\n5. **Focus Management on Failure**: Focus will remain unmanaged after rejection, leaving keyboard users without feedback or an obvious recovery path.\n\n*Comparison with findings*: All pre-commitment predictions were confirmed in the implementation.\n\n---\n\n## Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Missing label, unannounced errors, no `aria-describedby` or `aria-invalid` |\n| Keyboard-only | **MEDIUM** | Focus remains on file picker upon validation failure with no feedback; standard native activation works |\n| Low vision | **MEDIUM** | Error text appears conditionally without explicit contrast or sizing specs, constraints not documented |\n| Cognitive | **HIGH** | Vague error message (\"File too large\"), uncommunicated 5MB limit before attempt, no suggestion on how to remediate |\n| Vestibular & motion | **LOW** | No animations, transitions, or autoplaying elements |\n| Auditory access | **LOW** | No media elements or audio feedback |\n| Environmental contrast | **MEDIUM** | Potential contrast issues on `.error-message` depending on external styling; relies on external CSS |\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### Critical Findings\n\n1. **Input completely lacks an accessible name and programmatic label**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-25`\n   - **Element**: `<input type=\"file\" ... />` and `<div>Upload file</div>`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users, speech recognition / voice control users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships - Level A), SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Voice control users cannot say \"click upload file\" to target the input, and screen reader users only hear \"Choose File, button\" without knowing what file is being requested. A `<div>` is ignored by the accessibility tree as a labeling element. Note that user-agent intrinsic labels (\"Choose File\") do not provide context or replace an accessible label.\n   - **Fix**: Replace `<div>Upload file</div>` with `<label htmlFor=\"file-upload-input\">Upload file</label>` and add `id=\"file-upload-input\"` to the `<input>`.\n\n2. **Validation error state and message are not programmatically associated or communicated**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:21-28`\n   - **Element**: `<input type=\"file\" />` and `<div className=\"error-message\">{error}</div>`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users, cognitive accessibility users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.1 (Error Identification - Level A), SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A), SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages - Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When the user selects a file over 5MB, a visual string appears below the input, but the input does not set `aria-invalid=\"true\"`, does not associate the message via `aria-describedby`, and does not emit an announcement. A screen reader user has zero awareness that the file was rejected.\n   - **Fix**: \n     - Add `id=\"file-error\"` and `role=\"alert\"` (or `aria-live=\"assertive\"`) to the error container.\n     - Add `aria-invalid={error ? \"true\" : \"false\"}` and `aria-describedby={error ? \"file-error\" : undefined}` (or combine with help text ID) to `<input>`.\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: file_input_missing_label_and_error_association\nfingerprint: c4f81a7b8e2190ef\nsource: BuggyFileInput.jsx\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.1, SC 3.3.1, SC 4.1.2\nsection_508_fpc_context: Revised Section 508 / WCAG 2.0 A/AA (conforming requires 1.3.1, 3.3.1, 4.1.2)\nseverity: CRITICAL\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, cognitive=HIGH, keyboard=MEDIUM\nevidence: BuggyFileInput.jsx:19-28: <div>Upload file</div> followed by unlabelled <input type=\"file\"> and unassociated <div className=\"error-message\">\nreproduction_steps: \n  1. Inspect accessibility tree for <input type=\"file\">.\n  2. Notice accessible name is either empty or UA default (\"Choose file\"), not \"Upload file\".\n  3. Select a file larger than 5MB.\n  4. Inspect input attributes: aria-invalid is absent; aria-describedby is absent; error <div> has no role=\"alert\" or aria-live.\nexpected_behavior: Input has accessible name \"Upload file\", aria-invalid=\"true\" on error, and aria-describedby pointing to error message that is announced to AT.\nactual_behavior: Input has no programmatic label, error is visually displayed only with no AT association or announcement.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings\n\n1. **Undisclosed constraints and lack of descriptive error remediation**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:9-10`, `21-25`\n   - **Element**: `handleFileChange` size check (`file.size > 5000000`) and message (`'File too large'`)\n   - **Impacted Users**: Cognitive accessibility users, screen reader users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.2 (Labels or Instructions - Level A), SC 3.3.3 (Error Suggestion - Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Users are not informed of the 5MB file size limit or accepted file formats (.pdf, .doc, .docx) before selecting a file. Furthermore, when triggered, \"File too large\" does not specify the limit or how to resolve it (e.g., \"File exceeds maximum size of 5MB. Please upload a smaller PDF or Word document.\").\n   - **Fix**: Provide persistent help text linked via `aria-describedby` specifying the supported formats and maximum file size (5MB). Update error text to specify the allowed maximum size.\n\n2. **Selected file state is not communicated to assistive technology**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyFileInput.jsx:12`\n   - **Element**: `setSelectedFile(file)`\n   - **Impacted Users**: Screen reader users.\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.2 SC 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value - Level A), SC 4.1.3 (Status Messages - Level AA).\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: While native file inputs expose the selected filename to some AT upon query, replacing or clearing files dynamically or receiving success confirmation has no polite live status announcement or visible confirmation widget in the DOM.\n   - **Fix**: Render confirmation or file info associated with the input or a polite live region upon successful file selection.\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings\n\n- **Missing input `id` / wrapper relationship**: The wrapper `div className=\"file-upload\"` does not use fieldset/group semantics if part of a larger form, and lacks unique ID references for form controls.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing\n\n1. **Explicit programmatic association**: Missing `<label htmlFor=\"...\">` and `<input id=\"...\">`.\n2. **Help/Instruction text**: Missing visible and programmatic instructions detailing maximum file size (5MB) and accepted types prior to submission.\n3. **Error association and announcement**: Missing `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, and `role=\"alert\"`.\n4. **Actionable error suggestion**: Missing explicit limit clarification in error text (\"File too large\" vs \"File must be smaller than 5MB\").\n\n---\n\n## Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen Reader User**: Experiences a detached control. The control is identified only as a file upload button with no context about what is being uploaded. Errors appear visually but remain completely silent to the screen reader.\n- **Keyboard-only User**: Can activate the native file dialog using Space/Enter. However, when an invalid file is chosen, focus remains on the input without clear keyboard-navigable feedback indicating failure.\n- **Low Vision User**: Unclear whether the error message meets 4.5:1 text contrast. Because instructions are missing upfront, users zooming to 200% must repeatedly trigger trial-and-error uploads.\n- **Cognitive Accessibility**: High friction due to unstated requirements and unhelpful error messaging (\"File too large\" rather than stating the 5MB limit).\n\n---\n\n## Verdict Justification\n**REJECT**: The component fails baseline WCAG 2.2 Level A criteria (1.3.1, 3.3.1, 4.1.2) and Level AA criteria (3.3.3, 4.1.3). The core state (error) and identification (label) are completely decoupled from assistive technology, blocking access for screen reader and voice control users.\n\n---\n\n## Remediated Code Example\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useId } from 'react';\n\nconst AccessibleFileInput = () => {\n  const [selectedFile, setSelectedFile] = useState(null);\n  const [error, setError] = useState(null);\n\n  const inputId = useId();\n  const helpId = `${inputId}-help`;\n  const errorId = `${inputId}-error`;\n\n  const MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES = 5 * 1024 * 1024; // 5MB\n\n  const handleFileChange = (e) => {\n    const file = e.target.files[0];\n    if (file && file.size > MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES) {\n      setError('File exceeds maximum size of 5MB. Please choose a smaller file.');\n      setSelectedFile(null);\n    } else {\n      setSelectedFile(file || null);\n      setError(null);\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"file-upload\">\n      <label htmlFor={inputId} className=\"file-upload-label\">\n        Upload document\n      </label>\n      \n      <p id={helpId} className=\"file-upload-help\">\n        Accepted formats: PDF, DOC, DOCX. Maximum file size: 5MB.\n      </p>\n\n      <input\n        id={inputId}\n        type=\"file\"\n        onChange={handleFileChange}\n        accept=\".pdf,.doc,.docx\"\n        aria-invalid={error ? 'true' : 'false'}\n        aria-describedby={error ? `${errorId} ${helpId}` : helpId}\n      />\n\n      {error && (\n        <div id={errorId} className=\"error-message\" role=\"alert\">\n          {error}\n        </div>\n      )}\n\n      {selectedFile && !error && (\n        <p className=\"file-status\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n          Selected file: {selectedFile.name}\n        </p>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default AccessibleFileInput;\n```\n",
